WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.619
This video shows how to create subjects in the Omnichannel contact center:

00:00:05.619 --> 00:00:10.468
an outbound subject for calls you make, an inbound subject for calls customers

00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:15.260
make, the fields an agent fills in, and the settings of an automated subject.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.913
A subject is what a conversation is about:

00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:26.349
a sales call, a support request, a welcome call.

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:29.720
Each one has its own fields, campaign and flow.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:36.939
A subject is either outbound, work you start, or inbound, work the customer starts.

00:00:36.939 --> 00:00:43.190
Inbound work can be manual, logged by an agent, or automated, answered by an AI.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.514
Because the subject carries the fields and the flow, every activity of that

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:50.490
kind is handled the same way.

00:00:54.675 --> 00:00:58.552
Open Interaction Center, Management, Subject Flows.

00:00:58.552 --> 00:01:03.381
With no subjects yet, the page asks you to create a content type.

00:01:03.381 --> 00:01:08.007
A subject is a content type with the Omnichannel Subject part.

00:01:08.007 --> 00:01:11.135
Enter its display name and click Create.

00:01:11.586 --> 00:01:16.622
On the Add Parts page, click Add and Configure next to Omnichannel Subject.

00:01:16.622 --> 00:01:19.606
The subject's settings open straight away.

00:01:20.057 --> 00:01:22.544
Direction is Outbound by default.

00:01:22.544 --> 00:01:27.583
Pick a default campaign, used when an activity is created outside a load,

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:29.241
for example by hand.

00:01:29.241 --> 00:01:34.917
Require a disposition is on, because the disposition is what runs the subject flow.

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:38.552
Leave it on unless the subject is a one-way notice.

00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:39.637
Click Save.

00:01:43.842 --> 00:01:48.617
The Subject Flows list shows each subject with a badge for its direction,

00:01:48.617 --> 00:01:51.397
and Missing flow until it has an action.

00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:56.535
Edit Settings reopens the settings, Edit Content Type opens the whole type, and

00:01:56.535 --> 00:01:58.530
Manage Flow opens the flow.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.552
Open Edit Content Type, and click Add Field.

00:02:02.002 --> 00:02:06.190
Give the field a name, pick its type, here a text field, and save.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:10.902
The agent fills in the fields of the subject while completing the activity.

00:02:15.105 --> 00:02:21.465
Click Add Subject, create another content type, and add the Omnichannel Subject part the same way.

00:02:22.591 --> 00:02:26.040
Choose Inbound, and two more settings appear.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.533
Interaction type is Manual, when an agent logs the call, or Automated, when an AI answers.

00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:34.562
Channel is Phone or SMS.

00:02:34.562 --> 00:02:39.701
For outbound subjects these are chosen when the activities are loaded.

00:02:40.153 --> 00:02:46.736
The list now shows the inbound subject next to the outbound one, both marked Missing flow.

00:02:46.736 --> 00:02:49.273
Next, give each subject a flow.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:58.180
An automated inbound subject also asks for the address it answers on, and

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:02.470
with the AI features on, the AI profile, the subject goal, and the

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.853
speech models and voice for calls.

00:03:05.603 --> 00:03:09.816
It can let the AI update the contact or the subject, sets the

00:03:09.816 --> 00:03:15.853
no-response timeout, the response delay, and the words that opt a customer out, like STOP.

00:03:16.603 --> 00:03:20.981
A Live agent handoff card lets the AI pass the conversation to a

00:03:20.981 --> 00:03:25.109
person in a queue when the customer asks for one, is a ready

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:26.923
lead, or is frustrated.

00:03:31.123 --> 00:03:34.843
One outbound subject for each kind of call your team makes.

00:03:35.593 --> 00:03:39.333
An inbound subject to log the calls customers make.

00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:44.163
Fields that capture exactly what each conversation needs.

00:03:44.913 --> 00:03:49.013
Automated subjects for an AI to answer texts and calls.

00:03:51.013 --> 00:03:55.232
Create a subject for each goal of a conversation, give it the fields

00:03:55.232 --> 00:03:59.737
it needs, and then build its flow, so that every outcome has a next step.

00:03:59.737 --> 00:04:04.070
The user manual and the technical guide are linked in the description.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.553
Thanks for watching.

